Z||000000||mrgone||07-27-2001||09:03 PM||||i spotted a fiero at a dealership not too far from me and had to check it out. pushed my car off the ramps and bump started it, (dead batt and starter on floor) and headed out. Its an 85 gt, auto, air, defrost, pm, pw, sunroof, spoiler, and some newer delco cassette deck. pushed down on front and rear -much more resistant than my car. checked for rust (on my knees) in the usual places (using my rustbox fiero i drove there as a guide) no visible trunk rust from what i could see, steering damper shock isnt too bad. the floor plugs were solid, the rad harness was solid. i was thinking this was either stored for a few or was a us car. BUT. it had 140kmph speedo.<BR>Is that right for a GT?<P>oh and get this--- 384,000 kms on the odometer. whoa!    what do you think about that?    my car has 241,000 on it and its wayyy rusted out. this car was in a very non rusted state. the a-arms(?) were smooth and grey like they should be, without any surface rust at all.   states car or summer only maybe..<P>i should check it out when the dealership is open, check the codes and ask about its history. if the car is cheap.... man, that would be a sweet upgrade from a 86 2m4 5 speed that i sunk 3000$ into. im not happy that its an auto though.... if it was a 4spd id be hardcore serious.<P>so tomorrow maybe ill drop my car off at the shop to get a new batt and starter intstalled so i can go over there and check the codes, check for blow-by, and maybe test drive the sucker.<P>i LOVE gt notchbacks<P>could someone do a carfax for me?<P>1G2PG3798FP25007<P>SHOOT!! thers a # missing in the vin... il check it out again tomorrow maybe<P><BR>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_9.jpg">    <BR><B>86.5 2m4 5speed turd 241,000kms</B><p>[This message has been edited by mrgone (edited 07-27-2001).]||||reg||1
