Z||000005||GT-maniac||07-27-2001||11:47 PM||||Well I seriously doubt it's an american car if the speedo's in kph. 140 is right though that's what my canadian 85 GT has too. It's one thing I really don't like about the 85's as everyone knows a fiero will do a lot better than 140 :^). That and it's only in metric not both. My car has supposedly 110,000 km on it though it's on it's 3rd motor that I know of. My car originally came from Ontario where it was garage kept and not winter driven. As a result I only have minor surface rust on the frame and no holes. Hard too believe anyone put that many miles on a fiero though. Most of the members here seem to have less than 200,000 miles ( or 320,000 km's ) on their cars. If you can get it for a good price I'd say go for it. It will be a nice upgrade even with the auto.<BR>I love mine, it's not the fastest car around but it sure is fun.||||reg||1
